# Normalise text to LF in the repository, native on checkout.
* text=auto

# cmd.exe is the exception: it reads batch files line by line and expects CRLF.
# A .bat checked out with LF endings still runs on most machines, but the
# tolerance is undocumented and version-dependent, and the failure mode when it
# does bite is a launcher that silently does the wrong thing rather than one that
# refuses to start. These are the files an engineer double-clicks, so pin them
# regardless of what a given machine has core.autocrlf set to.
#
# The last matching pattern wins, so these must stay below the `* text=auto`
# line above or they are overridden by it.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Windows shortcuts and icons are binary; never touch their bytes.
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.pdf binary
*.xlsx binary
